  "html": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en-US\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Should I Water My Garden Today? | Chris Izworski</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Check whether to water today using recent rain, forecast drying, soil context and your garden inputs. For U.S. cities and ZIP codes.\">\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://chrisizworski.com/national-tools/garden-water/\">\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index,follow,max-image-preview:large\">\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Should I Water My Garden Today? | Chris Izworski\">\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"A live U.S. garden watering decision built from observed rain, recent drying, forecast rain and mapped soil context.\">\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\">\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://chrisizworski.com/national-tools/garden-water/\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary\">\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/assets/national-garden-water.css?v=20260904-v5\">\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@graph\":[{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"@id\":\"https://chrisizworski.com/#person\",\"name\":\"Chris Izworski\",\"url\":\"https://chrisizworski.com/\"},{\"@type\":\"WebApplication\",\"name\":\"Garden Water Today\",\"applicationCategory\":\"UtilitiesApplication\",\"operatingSystem\":\"Any\",\"isAccessibleForFree\":true,\"url\":\"https://chrisizworski.com/national-tools/garden-water/\",\"description\":\"A U.S. garden watering decision using observed NOAA weather, National Weather Service forecast signals, and USDA mapped soil context.\",\"author\":{\"@id\":\"https://chrisizworski.com/#person\"},\"publisher\":{\"@id\":\"https://chrisizworski.com/#person\"},\"dateModified\":\"2026-09-08\"}]}</script>\n<meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"Should I Water My Garden Today? | Chris Izworski\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"A live U.S. garden watering decision built from observed rain, recent drying, forecast rain and mapped soil context.\">\n</head>\n<body>\n<header class=\"site-head\">\n  <div class=\"head-in\">\n    <a class=\"brand\" href=\"/\">Chris Izworski</a>\n    <nav class=\"nav\" aria-label=\"Primary\">\n      <a href=\"/\">Home</a>\n      <a href=\"/tools/\">Michigan Tools</a>\n      <a href=\"/national-tools/\">U.S. Outdoor Tools</a>\n      <a href=\"/national-tools/garden/\" aria-current=\"page\">Garden Tools</a>\n    </nav>\n  </div>\n</header>\n\n<main class=\"body\">\n  <div class=\"breadcrumb\"><a href=\"/\">Home</a> &rsaquo; <a href=\"/national-tools/\">U.S. Outdoor Tools</a> &rsaquo; Garden Water</div>\n  <div class=\"tk\">Live data · United States</div>\n  <h1>Should I water my garden today?</h1>\n  <p class=\"sub\">Enter a city or ZIP. The tool replays observed rain and recent drying, checks what is coming next, and gives you a plain watering decision instead of another weather dashboard.</p>\n\n  <section class=\"lookup\" aria-label=\"Garden location\">\n    <form id=\"location-form\" class=\"location-form\">\n      <label for=\"location\">Where is your garden?</label>\n      <div class=\"location-row\">\n        <input id=\"location\" name=\"location\" placeholder=\"City or ZIP\" autocomplete=\"postal-code\" required>\n        <button class=\"btn\" type=\"submit\">Check today</button>\n      </div>\n      <button class=\"location-link\" id=\"use-location\" type=\"button\">Use my location</button>\n      <div class=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div>\n    </form>\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"result\" id=\"result\" hidden aria-live=\"polite\">\n    <div class=\"result-place\" id=\"place\">Your garden</div>\n    <div id=\"decision-content\">\n    <div class=\"tk tk-season\">Today's call</div>\n    <h2 class=\"decision\" id=\"decision\">—</h2>\n    <p class=\"amount\" id=\"amount\">—</p>\n    <p class=\"why\" id=\"why\"></p>\n\n    <div class=\"signal-grid\" aria-label=\"Signals behind today's call\">\n      <div class=\"signal\"><span>Recent observed rain</span><strong id=\"recent-rain\">—</strong><small id=\"recent-rain-source\">—</small></div>\n      <div class=\"signal\"><span>Rain, next 24h</span><strong id=\"forecast-rain\">—</strong><small>NWS forecast amount</small></div>\n      <div class=\"signal\"><span>Water demand today</span><strong id=\"demand\">—</strong><small>Crop-adjusted ET</small></div>\n      <div class=\"signal\"><span>Mapped soil</span><strong id=\"soil-read\">—</strong><small>USDA context</small></div>\n    </div>\n\n    <p class=\"next-line\"><strong>Check again:</strong> <span id=\"next-check\">—</span></p>\n    <p class=\"assumption\" id=\"assumption-line\"></p>\n\n    </div>\n    <details class=\"adjustments\" id=\"adjustments\">\n      <summary>Adjust this result for my garden</summary>\n      <p id=\"adjustment-error\" role=\"alert\" hidden></p>\n      <form id=\"adjust-form\">\n        <div class=\"adjust-grid\">\n          <label>Crop\n            <select id=\"crop\"></select>\n          </label>\n          <label>Growth stage\n            <select id=\"stage\">\n              <option value=\"seedling\">Seedling / new transplant</option>\n              <option value=\"developing\">Developing</option>\n              <option value=\"mature\" selected>Established / mature</option>\n            </select>\n          </label>\n          <label>Garden type\n            <select id=\"bed\">\n              <option value=\"ground\" selected>In ground</option>\n              <option value=\"raised\">Raised bed</option>\n              <option value=\"container\">Container</option>\n            </select>\n          </label>\n        </div>\n        <label class=\"rain-override\">Rain in my gauge, past 72 hours (optional)\n          <input id=\"rain-gauge\" type=\"number\" inputmode=\"decimal\" min=\"0\" max=\"10\" step=\"0.05\" placeholder=\"Use observed weather\">\n          <small>Use this when your gauge is a better read on a localized storm than nearby stations. Daily weather records approximate the 72-hour window; exact rain timing is unknown.</small>\n        </label>\n        <label class=\"checkline\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"watered-recently\"> <span>I watered in the past 7 days</span></label>\n        <div class=\"irrigation-fields\" id=\"irrigation-fields\" hidden>\n          <label>When?<input id=\"irrigation-date\" type=\"date\"></label>\n          <label>About how much?<select id=\"irrigation-amount\"><option value=\"0.25\">¼ inch</option><option value=\"0.5\" selected>½ inch</option><option value=\"0.75\">¾ inch</option><option value=\"1\">1 inch</option></select></label>\n        </div>\n        <button class=\"btn secondary\" type=\"submit\">Update my result</button>\n      </form>\n    </details>\n\n    <p class=\"source-line\" id=\"source-line\"></p>\n  </section>\n\n  <section class=\"explain\">\n    <h2 class=\"sh\">What goes into the call</h2>\n    <div class=\"explain-grid\">\n      <article class=\"explain-card\"><div class=\"tk\">Water in</div><h3>Observed and incoming rain</h3><p>Recent NOAA and NWS observations are reconciled before the decision. Forecast probability is never turned into an invented rainfall amount.</p></article>\n      <article class=\"explain-card\"><div class=\"tk\">Water out</div><h3>Recent drying and today's demand</h3><p>Observed temperatures drive the recent water-loss ledger. NWS reference evapotranspiration is preferred for today's atmospheric demand.</p></article>\n      <article class=\"explain-card\"><div class=\"tk\">Water storage</div><h3>Soil and root-zone context</h3><p>USDA mapped soil and crop rooting depth estimate storage. The tool carries uncertainty as a range rather than pretending it measured your soil moisture.</p></article>\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"model-note\">This is a weather-and-soil decision model, not a soil-moisture sensor. If you watered recently or have a rain-gauge reading, add it under “Adjust this result for my garden.”</p>\n  </section>\n</main>\n<footer class=\"footer\"><div class=\"footer-in\">© 2026 <a href=\"/\">Chris Izworski</a> · Free live tools built from public data.</div></footer>\n<script type=\"module\" src=\"/assets/national-garden-water-page.js?v=20260904-v5\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
}
